<title>LITHUANIA: TOTAL STATE DEBT AT 7.37 BLN LITAS.</title>
<headline>TOTAL STATE DEBT AT 7.37 BLN LITAS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's total state debt rose by 176 million litas to 7.37 billion litas in the first three months of 1997, finance minister Algirdas Shemetas told parliament on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The finance minister also said that the country's foreign loans as of April 1 stood at 4.7 billion litas, an increase of 39 million litas from the end of 1996.</p>
<p>He added that the country's internal debt rose to 2.65 billion litas in the same period, an increase of 137 million litas.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, +370 2 22 35 17</p>
